#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/update-troubleshooting.rst:7
#: 5d3feb43b6124a2694f6294bc40aa010
msgid ""
"\"Failed to synchronize cache for repo\" errors when updating Fedora "
"templates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/update-troubleshooting.rst:10
#: f4242154fc834f6099af642bbbd725af
msgid ""
"This is a general Fedora issue, not one that is Qubes-specific. Usually, the "
"issue is due to network problems (especially if downloading updates over "
"Tor) or problems with the download mirrors. Often, the problem can be "
"resolved by trying again on a different connection (a different Tor circuit, "
"if using Tor) or waiting and trying again later. Sometimes you may need to "
"clear the dnf cache. Here are some examples of non-Qubes reports about this "
"problem:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/update-troubleshooting.rst:12
#: 6cf61380b01b4d089b7527138fe46562
msgid ""
"https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/issues-with-dnf-upgrade-on-fedora-30-"
"failed-to-synchronize-cache-for-repo/71681"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/update-troubleshooting.rst:14
#: 110e8b51d17a4d79a14bfa769cf6d99f
msgid ""
"https://unix.stackexchange.com/questions/390805/repos-not-working-on-fedora-"
"error-failed-to-synchronize-cache-for-repo-update"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/update-troubleshooting.rst:16
#: 48d3c1e51fe946a18b3f09b0387de0d5
msgid ""
"https://www.reddit.com/r/Fedora/comments/74nldq/"
"fedora_26_dnf_error_failed_to_synchronize_cache/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/update-troubleshooting.rst:18
#: a14c87ae7f7541ba91c7e80842e0e4da
msgid "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1494178"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/update-troubleshooting.rst:20
#: 419eba697a664b23a8da3a6cda178c4d
msgid ""
"https://stackoverflow.com/questions/45318256/error-failed-to-synchronize-"
"cache-for-repo-updates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/update-troubleshooting.rst:24
#: 27814100077945a7b8da950f005f3fbb
msgid ""
"More examples can be found by searching for “Failed to synchronize cache for "
"repo” (with quotation marks) on your preferred search engine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/update-troubleshooting.rst:27
#: 122ea17123b040409ac608a905e291ba
msgid "Lost internet access after a template update"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/update-troubleshooting.rst:30
#: 95d2b875d60b4fb9bf5841d609db5bfb
msgid ""
"In earlier versions of Qubes, there were situations where qubes lost "
"internet access after a template update. The following fix should be applied "
"in recent versions of Qubes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/update-troubleshooting.rst:32
#: a23adde9d3984c3286ef19b1ea3e2e27
msgid ""
"Run ``systemctl enable NetworkManager-dispatcher.service`` in the template "
"upon which your NetVM is based. You may have to reboot afterward for the "
"change to take effect. (**Note:** This is an upstream problem. See `this "
"Redhat ticket <https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=974811>`__). For "
"details, see the qubes-users mailing list threads `here <https://"
"groups.google.com/d/topic/qubes-users/xPLGsAJiDW4/discussion>`__ and `here "
"<https://groups.google.com/d/topic/qubes-users/uN9G8hjKrGI/discussion>`__.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/update-troubleshooting.rst:35
#: 5450a3e0141f493bbb53d8595f2bb312
msgid "Windows update is stuck"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/update-troubleshooting.rst:38
#: 3d1263e3ad774e139a2b1db97b7bd433
msgid ""
"This has nothing to do with Qubes. It’s a longstanding Windows bug. More "
"information about this issue and solutions can be found `here <https://"
"superuser.com/questions/951960/windows-7-sp1-windows-update-stuck-checking-"
"for-updates>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/update-troubleshooting.rst:41
#: 643ae72cf89b4dba978ed23e99bf0e21
msgid "Dom0 and/or template update stalls when updating via the GUI tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/update-troubleshooting.rst:44
#: a88ba5ec62c3471191873e7a548d4563
msgid "This can usually be fixed by updating via the command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/update-troubleshooting.rst:46
#: 0e27b89fc5e34daa87164ef7f63528f0
msgid "In dom0, open a terminal and run ``sudo qubes-dom0-update``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/troubleshooting/update-troubleshooting.rst:48
#: ffc94a24e75d49b4b7e903ee2f7cccd4
msgid ""
"Depending on your operating system, open a terminal in the templates and run:"
msgstr ""

